# Buttons

Use `@/components/ui/Button` for every visible action. Do not style a raw `<button>` or `<a>` as a CTA.

## Anatomy

- Shape: `rounded-full` (pill). Never square or `rounded-md` CTAs.
- Typeface: **Montserrat** (`font-heading`) semibold, slight tracking.
- Touch target: at least 40px (`sm` = `h-10`). Prefer `md` in forms, `lg` on marketing heroes.
- Motion: 200ms lift on hover. Disabled = no lift, 55% opacity, `cursor-not-allowed`.
- Loading: set `loading` — spinner + `disabled`. Do not swap the label for the word “Loading…”.

## Variants (pick one, do not invent colors)

| Variant | Use |
|---|---|
| `primary` | One main action per view (save, submit, get started) |
| `secondary` | Supporting navy action |
| `outline` | Secondary / cancel / print |
| `ghost` | Tertiary on light surfaces |
| `danger` | Destructive only (reject, delete) |
| `inverse` | On navy / photo heroes (white fill) |
| `ghostDark` | On navy / photo heroes (glass) |

Never put two `primary` buttons side by side. Pair `primary` + `outline`, or `inverse` + `ghostDark`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-3 py-1 text-white">Save</button>
<Button variant="primary">Save</Button>
<Button variant="primary">Cancel</Button>

// ✅ GOOD
<Button type="submit" loading={saving}>Save record</Button>
<Button variant="outline" type="button">Cancel</Button>
<Button size="lg" variant="inverse">Start as a patient</Button>
```

## Do not

- Override `rounded-full`, `font-heading`, or height unless the control is an icon-only chrome button (menu, close, bell).
- Use `danger` for navigation or “log out”.
- Nest a `Button` inside another button. Wrap with `Link` outside.
